# LOOP LEDGER

Workspace: {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Append only, never rewrite history. One line per closed task, one line per call fired, one line per miss, one line per skill or job card used, one block per weekly review. Every line goes under Lines at the end of this file; the sections before it show the shapes. If the run log and the ledger disagree, the run log is the record and this file is the summary that got it wrong.

## Run logs

One file per task: `_log/LOOP-RUNLOG-<task>.md`. Append only, one line per event, timestamped:

```
| Time | Loop | Event | Detail |
```

Loop is which part of the graph wrote the line: run, workaround, hunt, review, tier check, call, rollback. At close the run log compresses into one task line below. Tasks below the small task floor skip the run log; their ledger line is the whole record.

