## Miss lines

One line per miss, written at Session Close. The literal word `Miss` in column two is the selector `icm-loop.sh` and `icm-forge` grep for. Sev: 3 wrong output shipped or a decision made on bad information, 2 cost time, 1 cosmetic, 2 when unsure. At fault is a rule book, job card or skill path exactly as it exists on disk, or the word `none`. A fault that returns after a patch starts its What missed with `RECURRENCE:`.

| Date | Miss | Sev | At fault | What missed | Fix that would have prevented it |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|

<!-- Example of a filled line:
| 2026-08-30 | Miss | 2 | _config/voice.md | shipped an em dash in deck copy | ban the em dash in deck copy, not just in prose |
-->

## Skill lines

One use line per skill or job card a task ran under, written at Session Close. `Use` in column two is the selector. Outcome is `ok`, `rework` or `abandoned`. Misses is how many miss lines this run wrote against it. One `Patched` line each time a human approves a proposal that changes a file; `icm-forge approve` writes it, and every miss dated before it counts as closed.

| Date | Use | Skill or job card | Path | Task | Outcome | Misses |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

| Date | Patched | Path | Proposal id |
