## Weekly review

Append one block per review, newest at the bottom, in exactly this shape:

```
Week of: <date>
Calls fired: <n> Necessary: <n>
Pre-mortem catches: <n> Hunt catches: <n> Review catches: <n> Audit catches: <n>
Workarounds taken: <n> Recurring blocker: <none, or the blocker and the proposed system fix>
Anchor decay check: <pass or what drifted>
Floor misses: <n tasks with more process lines than output>
Threshold proposals: <none, or the proposal and the operator's decision>
```

The trendline to watch: review and audit catches falling while pre-mortem and hunt catches hold. That is the graph learning, holes dying earlier where they are cheapest. Review catches rising means the hunt questions have gone stale, so update them with the patterns that slipped through. A blocker appearing twice in the workaround column is a system hole: build the fix once as its own task, stop paying the toll.

Anything the review wants changed in a rule book goes to `_log/FORGE-PROPOSALS.md` as a proposal. It does not get edited into `_config/` from here.

